  "spans": [
    {
      "id": "s1",
      "nodeId": "n3",
      "text": "Out of those, the study found that 65% contained arsenic, 36% had lead, 60% had BPA (industrial chemical bisphenol A) and 58% contained cadmium, a natural toxic metal typically found in plant soil and smoking products.",
      "contextBefore": "s from a new study released Wednesday. The 530 baby products, purchased in the past five months, were all tested by the Clean Label Project, a nonprofit group that advocates for transparent labeling. ",
      "contextAfter": " Some of the more popular brands that tested positive for these harmful ingredients, including Gerber, Enfamil, Plum Organics and Sprout, were the worst offenders, according to the study. The brands s",
      "start": 309,
      "end": 527,
      "extractSha256": "9429be2ce8de5f1ab2f5110ffc3b6e2e23e4508c45a23bdd0897cc1344e54473",
      "windowSha256": "ec10208ae44e7b93d04ce31c6b7afbbff0eee041afa6350f5e9c9f6e4e538373",
      "fetchedAt": "2026-11-18T03:12:19.645Z",
      "waybackUrl": "https://web.archive.org/web/20171026043717/https://www.nydailynews.com/life-style/popular-baby-formulas-foods-arsenic-lead-bpa-article-1.3587740",
      "tier": "exact"
    },
    {
      "id": "s2",
      "nodeId": "n4",
      "text": "The single oral dose of arsenic trioxide was further followed by excretion of an amount of arsenic equivalent to about 60% of the administered dose: 49% in the urine and 11% in the feces.",
      "contextBefore": "single oral dose of arsenic trioxide was such that inorganic arsenic and MAA occured chiefly in the blood cells; DMAA, chiefly in the plasma; and the arsenic compounds disappeared rapidly from blood. ",
      "contextAfter": " In the other words, more arsenic tended to be excreted in theurine. DMAA accounted for the major portion of arsenic excreted in the urine and feces, and this finding re-confirmed that DMAA is the maj",
      "start": 1434,
      "end": 1621,
      "extractSha256": "608dba7eda309c3238ec1343f4c8074178340c04600b95ec22b944f356997cd7",
      "windowSha256": "c78d53bb31624171c8d0c7379942cd5ab414528829cc9b9896d15e8c443cc743",
      "fetchedAt": "2026-11-18T03:12:24.317Z",
      "waybackUrl": null,
      "tier": "exact"
    },
    {
      "id": "s3",
      "nodeId": "n5",
      "text": "In most animal studies, DMA has been the main metabolite, while in humans, urinary excretion analysis under normal conditions have revealed approximately 20% inorganic arsenic, 20% MMA, and 60% DMA [13,14].",
      "contextBefore": "cal species present in the body. It is generally recognized that inorganic arsenic is more toxic than organic arsenic (DMA and MMA), and among inorganic arsenic, As3+ is more toxic than As5+ [10-12]. ",
      "contextAfter": " Therefore, arsenic levels measured in the urine can be used as a biomarker of arsenic exposure in humans. Since arsenic is rapidly metabolized and excreted through the urine, this measurement can pro",
      "start": 8988,
      "end": 9194,
      "extractSha256": "50a9ac5325e82668e11abec4ca2be212566da4141d6ef89b140f41e408ca6d84",
      "windowSha256": "fa548787339eceffe3cb4837f9916e8ca47d6fe4d36b459b084b85b015be4d7c",
      "fetchedAt": "2026-11-18T03:12:25.512Z",
      "waybackUrl": "https://web.archive.org/web/20180602124351/https://www.jpmph.org/journal/view.php?doi=10.3961%2Fjpmph.14.036",
      "tier": "exact"
